{"context":"ADR-017 made `eka.yaml` the repository identity but preserved a **LEGACY mode**: repositories without `eka.yaml` were still registerable/syncable via path/basename resolution. Three problems follow:\n\n1. **Non-EKA directories \"succeed\".** Because of the legacy mode, `eka project register` and `eka sync` succeed on directories that are not EKA repositories at all (no `eka.yaml`, no docs tree). This is a confusing, git-less behavior — git refuses such directories with `fatal: not a git repository`; EKA accepts them.\n2. **`eka validate` scans the wrong scope.** The v1.1-era policy scans EVERY markdown file in the whole repository tree, including Markdown outside the knowledge/docs context. With the EKA Standard v2.0 the authoring layout is `docs/\u003cdimension\u003e/\u003ctype\u003e-\u003cid\u003e.json` and Markdown is a legacy adapter — the whole-tree sweep is misaligned, and a stray frontmatter-bearing `.md` anywhere in the tree can fail the whole repository (R2/R6/R7/R9 blocking rules). The report also labels the scanned count as \".md files\" while JSON authoring files are counted too.\n3. **Docs-in-repo is not an obligation.** Recent EKA standards no longer use docs-in-repo at all — the workspace store is canonical; docs-in-repo is ONLY a backward-compatibility (v1-style) authoring adapter, not an obligation.","decision":"### Decision 1 — `eka.yaml` is the mandatory repository marker (amends ADR-017 legacy mode)\n\n- An EKA repository = a directory tree carrying `eka.yaml` (located by the ADR-017 walk-up). **No legacy mode**: a repository without `eka.yaml` is NOT an EKA repository.\n- ALL repo-scoped commands refuse deterministically (git-style strictness) when the walk-up finds no `eka.yaml`: `eka sync` (+pull/push), `eka project register`, `eka export`, `eka import`, `eka new`, `eka publish`, `eka edit`, `eka discard`, `eka view`, `eka get`, `eka watch`. Core refusal sentence (each command wraps it in its house wording):\n\n  `\u003cabs\u003e is not an EKA repository (no eka.yaml); run 'eka init' first`\n\n  e.g. `eka: sync refused: /path is not an EKA repository (no eka.yaml); run 'eka init' first`.\n\n- Workspace-scoped commands stay ungated: `eka status`, `eka project list`, `eka draft list`, `eka integrity check` (they read the workspace store). `eka init` is the generator (creates `eka.yaml`) — ungated. `eka validate` is docs-scoped (Decision 2) and path-based — ungated.\n- The workspace library API keeps its legacy branches (`RegisterRepo`, exact-path `FindRepo`) as an **internal compatibility layer**; they are no longer reachable from any CLI command. The engine (`sync.Run`) and the commands enforce the gate.\n- Auto-registration semantics: `eka sync` on an unregistered METADATA repository still auto-registers from `eka.yaml` (ADR-017 §5.2 unchanged); the legacy basename auto-registration branch is **REMOVED**.\n\n### Decision 2 — conformance scope: docs tree only, skip when absent\n\n- `eka validate` (and the shared conformance gate used by `eka sync --from-docs` / `eka export` / `eka init` post-generation validation) scans ONLY the `\u003croot\u003e/docs` knowledge tree when it exists.\n- When `\u003croot\u003e/docs` does NOT exist: validation is **SKIPPED** — the report is a clean PASS (0 files, 0 artifacts, 0 errors) with a deterministic informational note:\n\n  `no docs/ knowledge tree — nothing to validate (docs-in-repo is legacy authoring — EKA v2 keeps knowledge in the workspace)`\n\n  NOT a refusal: docs-in-repo is optional backward compatibility.\n- The report count label is fixed: the scanned count includes `.json` authoring files, so the label becomes **\"authoring files\"** (was \".md files\").\n\n### Decision 3 — adoption: `eka.yaml` comes only from `eka init`\n\n- `eka init` remains the ONLY generator of `eka.yaml`. Adoption path for existing legacy repositories (docs/ tree, no `eka.yaml`): running `eka init` on them now GENERATES `eka.yaml` (identity: project/namespace = the deterministic default namespace derived from the directory basename, name = basename; the init output already instructs \"edit eka.yaml before the first sync to change it\"). Existing-eka runs that already have `eka.yaml` remain no-ops.\n- `eka.yaml` itself becomes an EKA-repository marker in bootstrap discovery (alongside the existing `docs/operating/` + `docs/exchange/` markers), so `eka init` on a metadata repository is a no-op (reuse plan) and never scaffolds the legacy docs skeleton into a v2 repository.\n- Migration note for existing stores with legacy registrations: after adoption, the first `eka sync` resolves the metadata identity; when the legacy registration used a different project/name, the identity lookup misses and the ADR-017 ownership/namespace rules produce the deterministic refusal — the fix is aligning `eka.yaml` (project/name/namespace) with the existing registration and re-syncing; the identity pair stays frozen after the first successful sync.","consequences":"- **Git-like strictness**: every repo-scoped command on a non-EKA directory fails fast with a deterministic message and a hint (`run 'eka init' first`).\n- **Verified refusal strings** (byte-exact; all carry the core sentence `\u003cabs\u003e is not an EKA repository (no eka.yaml); run 'eka init' first`):\n  - `eka: sync refused: …` (exit 2), `eka: project register failed: …` (exit 2), `eka: export refused: …` (exit 2), `eka: import failed: …` (exit 2), `eka: edit refused: …` (exit 2), `eka: discard refused: …` (exit 2);\n  - `eka: new: refused: …` (exit 1 — the authoring refusal class, with the colon), `eka: publish refused: …` (exit 1), `eka: view refused: …` (exit 1), `eka: get refused: …` (exit 1);\n  - `eka watch` renders the refusal frame `Not an EKA repository (no eka.yaml).` plus the run hint and keeps watching — no exit.\n- **Exit-code classes (verified)**: exit 1 = `new`, `publish`, `view`, `get`; exit 2 = `sync`, `project register`, `export`, `import`, `edit`, `discard`; `watch` = frame. The metadata-present-but-unregistered messages stay byte-identical (e.g. `eka: view refused: repository \u003cabs\u003e is not registered in the EKA workspace; run 'eka sync' (auto-registers) or 'eka project register' first`).\n- **Breaking change** (amends ADR-017 D2 + compatibility section): legacy repositories must adopt `eka.yaml` (via `eka init`) before repo-scoped commands work; existing workspace stores with legacy registrations migrate by adoption + aligning `eka.yaml`; the self-conformance gate for this repo becomes `eka validate reference/project` (the repo root has no docs/ tree → skip).\n- **Reference project unaffected**: already carries `eka.yaml` + `docs/`.\n- **Spec amendment required**: ADR-017's spec (`reference/spec-repository-identity.md`) sections describing the legacy path — D2 row, §4 \"if not found: legacy exact-path lookup\", §5.2 step 3, §7 breaking-change text — are amended in Phase C of the ADR-018 implementation; this ADR documents that requirement explicitly.\n\n### Compatibility \u0026 migration\n\n- **Legacy stores**: existing workspace stores with legacy registrations migrate by adoption — run `eka init` on the legacy repository (generates `eka.yaml`), align `eka.yaml` (project/name/namespace) with the existing registration, then re-sync; the first successful sync freezes the identity pair. A mismatched identity lookup produces the deterministic ADR-017 refusal, not a silent takeover.\n- **Refusal strings**: repo-scoped commands on a non-EKA directory emit `\u003cabs\u003e is not an EKA repository (no eka.yaml); run 'eka init' first` wrapped in each command's house wording (see the implementation spec §3, byte-pinned); exit code classes per command: `new`/`publish`/`view`/`get` = 1, `sync`/`project register`/`export`/`import`/`edit`/`discard` = 2; `watch` renders a refusal frame and keeps watching (no exit). The unregistered-metadata-repo case keeps exit 1 for `view`/`get`/`watch` (unchanged from today's `FindRepo` miss).\n- **Byte-identical**: the unregistered-metadata-repo refusal (`eka: \u003ccmd\u003e refused: repository \u003cabs\u003e is not in the EKA workspace; run 'eka sync' (auto-registers) or 'eka project register' first`), the ADR-013/ADR-015 gate behaviour for registered metadata repositories, and all workspace-scoped command output stay unchanged.\n- Implementation checklist and file-by-file details: `reference/spec-repository-context.md`.","alternativesConsidered":"- **Keep legacy mode forever** — rejected: no git-like strictness; non-EKA directories silently accepted by `register`/`sync`, which is the confusing behavior this ADR removes.\n- **Docs-in-repo as an obligation** — rejected: recent EKA standards don't use it; docs-in-repo is backward compatibility (v1 adapter), not an obligation — validation must skip, not refuse, when the tree is absent.\n- **Gate only `register`/`sync`** — rejected: inconsistent across repo-scoped commands; `new`/`publish`/`edit`/`discard`/`view`/`get`/`watch`/`export`/`import` on a non-EKA directory would keep the confusing behavior.\n- **A separate `--force`/`--adopt` flag for non-EKA registration** — rejected: complexity without a real use case; the deterministic adoption path (`eka init` generates `eka.yaml`) covers every scenario."}